    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-18614" textLabel="cytochrome P450 dependent diterpene olefin hydroxylase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="MONOMER-18614" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="355" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="O-28, hartmut">The cDNA for a diterpene olefin 3-hydroxylase from &lt;i&gt;Oryza sativa&lt;/i&gt; has been codon optimized and N-terminally modified and expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. The cytochrome P450 dependent monooxygenase (CYP701A8), also referred to as kauren oxidase-like (KOL4) is part of the kauren oxidase protein (KO) family involved in gibberellin biosynthesis but has undergone a neofunctionalization and shown to function in rice phytoalexin biosynthesis instead. KOL4 is able to hydroxylate |FRAME:CPD-4753 &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-sandaracopimaradiene| and |FRAME:CPD-4751 &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-cassa-12,15-diene| to yield the corresponding 3C&amp;alpha;-hydroxylated compounds, i.e. |FRAME:CPD-16610 &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-sandaracopimaradien-3&amp;beta;-ol| and |FRAME:CPD-16689 3&amp;alpha;-hydroxy-&lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-cassadiene|, respectively. KOL4 also added the 3C(&amp;alpha;)-oxy moiety to |FRAME:CPD1F-128 &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurene| yielding |FRAME:CPD-16690 3&amp;alpha;-hydroxy-&lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurene| indicating the deviation from the usual KO catalyzed C19 oxidation. However, the latter compound has no physiological relevance while the former two are potential intermediates in the biosynthesis of oryzalexin and phytocassane phytoalexins |CITS:[22247270]|. Although CYP701A8 reacts only poorly with |FRAME:CPD-16627 7&amp;beta;-hydroxy-&lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-sandaracopimaradiene| to form |FRAME:CPD-16612 oryzalexin D| it cannot ruled out as a possible branch of the biosynthetic route towards |FRAME:CPD-16612 oryzalexin D| |CITS:[23795884]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-18614" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Phytozome" value="Os06t0569500-01" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-N7F-69396, RXN-22718, RXN-22717, RXN-22716" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="Os06t0569500-01" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="G-18079" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_22247270" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_23795884" />
    </DataNode>
